# GitHub Actions Strategy

## Hard Limits

| Resource | Limit | Our Usage | % Used |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| GitHub Actions minutes (private repo) | 2,000/month | ~1,800/month | 90% |
| RSS feeds (29) | Unlimited | 1,740/day | FREE |

API providers (currentsapi, newsdata.io, contextualweb) are retained in code but **disabled**. Only RSS feeds run.

## Schedule

```
cron: '*/20 * * * *'   ← every 20 minutes (72 triggers/day)
IST schedule gate      ← Python step skips 12 triggers, 60 actual runs/day
```

### IST-Weighted Distribution (60 runs/day)

| IST Window | Hours | Runs | Gap (approx) | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 00:00–05:00 | 5h | 5 | ~60 min | Night low — minimal news publishing |
| 05:00–08:00 | 3h | 9 | ~20 min | Morning ramp — all slots |
| 08:00–11:00 | 3h | 9 | ~20 min | Morning peak — all slots |
| 11:00–14:00 | 3h | 8 | ~22 min | Lunch lull |
| 14:00–16:00 | 2h | 5 | ~24 min | Afternoon low |
| 16:00–19:00 | 3h | 9 | ~20 min | Evening peak — all slots |
| 19:00–22:00 | 3h | 9 | ~20 min | Night peak — all slots |
| 22:00–00:00 | 2h | 6 | ~20 min | Late evening — all slots |

### IST Gate Mechanism

The workflow triggers every 20 min (`:00`, `:20`, `:40` each hour = 72/day). The first step runs a Python IST gate that checks `S[hour]` for allowed minute slots. If the current slot isn't in the schedule, all subsequent steps are skipped via `if: steps.gate.outputs.SHOULD_RUN == 'true'`. Skipped runs cost ~15 sec each (~3 min/day overhead). `workflow_dispatch` (manual trigger) always bypasses the gate.

