## Rotation (daily totals)

| Provider | Calls/Day | Cost |
|----------|-----------|------|
| RSS feeds | 1,740 fetches | Free |
| Firebase writes | ~50–100 bundle docs | <0.5% of 20,000 |
| GitHub Actions | ~60 min/day (+ ~3 min skip overhead) | ~90% of 2,000/month |

## Content Pipeline (fetch_news.py)

```
Fetch (29 RSS) → Normalize → Dedup (3-layer) → Bundle (≤50/doc) → upload_bundles() → article_bundles
```

Short field names in each bundle: `i`=id, `t`=title, `d`=description, `img`=imageUrl, `u`=articleUrl, `p`=publishedAt (ms), `s`=sourceName, `c`=category, `tr`=trending (1 if trending, omitted otherwise)

### Deduplication Layers
1. **Article ID hash** — SHA-256 of (normalize_title(title) + normalized_source)
2. **URL dedup** — seen_urls set within RSS processing
3. **Cross-run cache** — `.article_cache.json` persisted via actions/cache

### URL-Based Category Override
After fetching from RSS, `url_derived_category(article_url, feed_category)` checks the article URL path against `URL_CATEGORY_SIGNALS` (defined after `RSS_FEEDS`). First match wins and overrides the feed-assigned category. Fixes RSS feeds that leak articles from other sections (e.g. abplive.com/education/feed publishing entertainment articles). Logs `[cat-fix]` to stdout when an override fires.

### Provider Tagging
Every article gets `_provider` key (`rss`).
Stripped before Firebase upload (short field mapping in `upload_bundles`).

### Category Short Codes (CATEGORY_SHORT dict)
RSS feeds use short codes directly in their `category` field.
7 merged short codes: `nat` (दुनिया), `spt` (खेल), `ent` (मनोरंजन), `bus` (व्यापार), `tec` (तकनीक), `hlt` (स्वास्थ्य), `edu` (शिक्षा).
App-side category expansion: nat→(nat,pol,cri), bus→(bus,stk), tec→(tec,sci). Single-category for spt, ent, hlt, edu.
International/world/defense categories removed — Indian RSS feeds cover all relevant news under `nat`.

### Quality Gate
MIN_DESC_LEN=250; description truncated to max 500 chars. Image rules unchanged.

### Trending
24h filter, Jaccard similarity clustering on stemmed Hindi title words (threshold 0.30), freq≥2 distinct sources. Lightweight Hindi stemmer strips common suffixes (ों, ें, ी, ा, े, etc.) so inflected forms match. `TRENDING_MIN_WORDS=3` filters short titles. Near-miss clusters logged when 0 qualify. Add `tr`:1 for trending articles only.

