## Run Metrics (logs/run_metrics.txt)

Cumulative totals updated after every run. Pushed to `Logs` branch (not `main`) to avoid branch protection conflicts.

Before `fetch_news.py`, the workflow fetches `origin/Logs` and restores `logs/run_metrics.txt` so totals accumulate across runs (`main` does not carry this file). After the run, metrics are copied to `/tmp`, the untracked path is removed (so `git checkout Logs` cannot fail), then committed on `Logs`. **`git stash` is not used** — stash only accepts tracked paths; the metrics file is untracked on `main`.

**Format:**
```
# Headlinr Metrics
# Updated: 2026-03-25 05:47:29 UTC
# Total Runs: 150

Total: 12345
Trending: 456

दुनिया: 1234
खेल: 567
मनोरंजन: 890
व्यापार: 2345
तकनीक: 456
स्वास्थ्य: 234
शिक्षा: 345
```

Each run adds its fresh article counts to the existing totals. Committed and pushed to `Logs` branch by the workflow via `github-actions[bot]`.

## Structured Summary (printed at end of each run)

Per-provider table (raw→dedup→quality→fresh), per-category breakdown with zero-coverage alerts, quality gate pass rate, trending cluster stats, freshness stats (cache before→after), and per-phase timing.

